 HISTORY                                                          7200 1451
 -------                                                          7200 1451
    This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction       7200 1451
    Physics (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. 7200 1451
    The thermal scattering law data for Plutonium in Plutonium    7200 1451
    Dioxide was developed using ab initio lattice dynamics        7200 1451
    (AILD)[1,2]. The PuO2 (space group 225) ground state          7200 1451
    structure is approximated in VASP with AFM-1K magnetic order  7200 1451
    and spin-orbit-coupling. Semi-itinerant Pu 5f electrons,      7200 1451
    hybridized with O 2p electrons, are modelled with an          7200 1451
    effective Hubbard term of 5 eV. A 500 eV plane-wave cutoff,   7200 1451
    9x9x9 k-mesh, GGA-PBEsol exhchange-correlations and Gaussian  7200 1451
    smearing ensure converged unit cell electronic structure.     7200 1451
    Phonon DOS were generated using a 2x2x2 supercell in PHONON   7200 1451
    using the dynamical-matrix method. Twelve temperatures are    7200 1451
    available in this library. The Full Law Analysis Scattering   7200 1451
    System Hub (FLASSH) system was used to produce File 7 MT = 2, 7200 1451
    4 data for Plutonium in PuO2 [3] reflecting natural Oxygen    7200 1451
    abundances [5], 100% Pu-239 and experimental lattice          7200 1451
    constants [6]. MAT=7200 and ZA=7300 are used for Pu-239 in    7200 1451
    PuO2.                                                         7200 1451
